Execute Phase D1 only.

Inspect existing profiles, projects, UI, and migrations.

BUILD USER PREFERENCES
- Primary niche.
- Up to five subniches.
- Audience.
- Region.
- Language.
- Preferred platforms.
- Content goal.
- Tone.
- Short-form duration preference.
- Long-form duration preference.
- Topics to avoid.

Support editing preferences later.
Changing preferences must invalidate incompatible pending
suggestions without deleting saved ideas.

DISCOVER SCREEN
Tabs:
- Short-form.
- Long-form.
- Saved.

Filters:
- Niche.
- Duration.
- Region/language.
- Content goal.
- Evidence type.

CARD STRUCTURE
- Title.
- Hook.
- Angle.
- Audience fit.
- Duration.
- Prompt.
- Outline.
- Evidence status.
- Evidence checked-at timestamp.

ACTIONS
Save, dismiss, replace, more-like-this, edit prompt, create project.

At this phase, demo cards must be labeled as demo content.
Do not imply live trends are connected.

DATA MODEL
Use suitable entities for:
- Discovery preferences.
- Idea batches.
- Idea proposals.
- Evidence references.
- Feedback.
- Saved ideas.
- Project links.

Use stable IDs and row-level security.

TEST
Preference persistence, user isolation, saved/dismissed states,
migration, responsive UI, and empty states.

ACCEPTANCE
Users can configure their niche and manage clearly labeled
idea cards without fabricated trend claims.

Stop after D1.
